From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] free quarantine: an invalid free says which check failed and whether the guest freed that pointer before

0006 turns a free glibc would abort on into a logged leak, but its line says only "no glibc chunk", and it stops after 20 lines, so PGR's real count (every run
shows 20) and the cause are unknown. Now each line names the first test the pointer fails (not 16-byte aligned, impossible chunk size, chunk outside its heap,
next chunk not in use = this chunk is free already, bad prev_size, glibc's tcache key = freed twice) and, with BERBERIS_LOG_FREES=1, whether the guest freed that
pointer before (the last 65536 frees are kept: pointer, the caller's x30, tid): "freed by the guest N frees earlier (caller ..), still waiting in the quarantine
ring / already released to glibc", or "never freed by the guest". With the variable up to 2000 invalid frees are described, and past the cap one count line is
written at each power of two; without it the cap stays 20 and nothing is recorded (one getenv). Behaviour of free is unchanged: the same pointers are refused.
Applies after 0024 (independent of 0025). Module libberberis_proxy_libc.

diff --git a/android_api/libc/free_quarantine.cc b/android_api/libc/free_quarantine.cc
